erts in chips, defence and deep-sea drilling gathered as China\u2019s scientific competition with the US intensifies\n\nAccording to state news agency Xinhua, the Communist Party\u2019s Central Committee and the State Council, China\u2019s cabinet, invited 60 experts to the seaside resort of Beidaihe from August 1 to 7.\n\nWhile Xinhua did not publish the full guest list, it named 15 participants.\n\nThey covered defence engineering, semiconductors, deep-sea equipment, artificial intelligence, particle astrophysics, advanced manufacturing, healthcare, the digital economy and more.\n\nThe selection suggests that Beijing is seeking to combine long-term basic research with efforts to address immediate technologica", "citation": "How the guest list for Beijing\u2019s summer retreat reveals its tech priorities \u2014 SCMP Economy, 2026-08-10. https://www.scmp.com/news/china/politics/article/3363523/how-guest-list-beijings-summer-retreat-reveals-its-tech-priorities?utm_source=rss_feed"}, {"title": "Global Market: Shanghai, Hong Kong stocks rise as consumer gains offset tech weakness", "feed": "ET Markets", "ts": "2026-08-10T07:47:16+00:00", "url": "https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/us-stocks/wall-street-guide/global-market-shanghai-hong-kong-stocks-rise-as-consumer-gains-offset-tech-weakness/articleshow/133090625.cms", "status": "ok", "excerpt": "Shanghai and Hong Kong stocks gained on Monday as consumer and property shares offset weakness in technology stocks. Investors assessed fresh Chinese inflation data, which pointed to persistent deflationary pressures, for clues on Beijing\u2019s policy outlook. Expectations of fiscal support and resilient exports also shaped market sentiment.\n\n(What's moving Sensex and Nifty Track latest market news, stock tips, Budget 2025, Share Market on Budget 2025 and expert advice, on ETMarkets. Also, ETMarkets.com is now on Telegram. For fastest news alerts on financial markets, investment strategies and stocks alerts, subscri